    "reason": "The historical change in PR #123949 modifies only whether a callee's `var_debug_info` is appended to the caller during MIR inlining. `var_debug_info` is pure debug metadata: it does not participate in execution, control flow, or dataflow, and the PR's own test changes merely add/remove `debug ... => ...` annotations in MIR dumps. The inliner still unconditionally merges source scopes and basic blocks, so there is no runtime-observable semantic divergence between the original unconditional append and the corrected gated append. Any Rust pair whose original/transformed functions return different values would have to invent an unrelated transformation (e.g. collapsing an assignment into a return slot or changing arithmetic), which violates the requirement to encode exactly the historical wrong transformation and not force a difference. Therefore no source-grounded counterexample pair can be validated for this metadata-only change.",
    "evidence": [],
    "attempts": 0
  },
  "analysis": {
    "evidence": [
      "At debuginfo=0, don't inline debuginfo when inlining",
      "caller_body.var_debug_info.append(&mut callee_body.var_debug_info);",
      "if self.tcx.sess.opts.debuginfo != DebugInfo::None {",
      "inline_mir_preserve_debug: Option<bool> = (None, parse_opt_bool, [TRACKED],",
      "when MIR inlining, whether to preserve debug info for callee variables",
      "people working on rust can build with or without debuginfo while",
      "still getting consistent results from the mir-opt tests.",
      "//@ compile-flags: -Zinline-mir-hint-threshold=1000 -C debuginfo=full",
      "//@ compile-flags: -C debuginfo=full",
      "//@ compile-flags: -Zpolymorphize=on -Zinline-mir=yes -C debuginfo=2",
      "// Note that as of PR#123949 this only crashes with debuginfo enabled",
      "// FIXME: always pass this after the next `#[cfg(bootstrap)]` update.",
      "Similarly, we need to keep debug info for functions inlined into other std functions,",
      "even if we're not going to output debuginfo for the crate we're currently building,",
      "so that it'll be available when downstream consumers of std try to use it.",
      "ptr align 4 %[[RET]], ptr align 4 %r, i64 12, i1 false",
      "CHECK-SAME: ptr{{.+}}sret{{.+}}%[[RET:.+]], ptr{{.+}}%r, ptr{{.+}}%v"
    ],
    "incorrectTransformation": "The historically incorrect transformation is unconditional appending of the callee's `var_debug_info` during inlining, regardless of `-C debuginfo=0`. The corrected behavior gates that append on debug info being enabled (`self.tcx.sess.opts.debuginfo != DebugInfo::None`), later generalized to `inline_mir_preserve_debug.unwrap_or(self.tcx.sess.opts.debuginfo != DebugInfo::None)`. `source_scopes` and basic blocks are still merged unconditionally; only debug-variable records are gated.",
    "inputDomain": "Rust MIR inlining: a caller is optimized with the MIR inliner enabled, and a callee with non-empty `var_debug_info` is selected for inlining. The distinguishing input condition is `-C debuginfo=0`/`DebugInfo::None` versus `-C debuginfo=full`, plus optionally `-Zinline-mir-preserve-debug`. Typical sources are small wrappers/helpers around `std::mem::replace`, range iteration, `Option` combinators, or `Step::forward`.",
    "kind": "optimization",
    "originalLogic": "In `Inliner::inline_call`, after extending caller locals and source scopes, the old code unconditionally merged the callee's debug variable records: `caller_body.var_debug_info.append(&mut callee_body.var_debug_info);`. Thus every successful MIR inlining copied the callee's `debug ... => ...` declarations into the caller even when the crate was compiled with no debug info.",
    "passIds": [
      "Inline"
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
      "`var_debug_info` affects only debug metadata and MIR size/compile work, not runtime semantics; do not expect control flow or program output to differ.",
      "Only `var_debug_info` is gated; `source_scopes` are still appended unconditionally, so inlined scopes can remain even when callee debug variables are absent.",
      "The decision is session-wide (`self.tcx.sess.opts...`), not per-callee or per-caller.",
      "`-Zinline-mir-preserve-debug` deliberately overrides debuginfo=0; std/bootstrap intentionally passes it so standard-library MIR is identical regardless of host debuginfo settings. Tests of the optimization must not pass this flag.",
      "Many MIR-opt tests were changed to add `-C debuginfo=full` so they continue checking inlined debug annotations; without it their expected diffs lose the `debug ...` lines.",
      "Forcing `-C debuginfo=full` can alter codegen output: tests had to adjust sret/argument names and memcpy operands, so codegen expectations are not invariant under this flag.",
      "The crash-test comment states the ICE only reproduces with debuginfo enabled; adding debuginfo to a test can expose unrelated crashes and must not be attributed to the inliner change."
