    "summary": "The MIR Inline pass should only copy a callee's `var_debug_info` into the caller when debug info is actually being emitted (debuginfo != None), unless `-Zinline-mir-preserve-debug` explicitly overrides this. Historically it appended callee debug variables unconditionally, growing caller MIR and doing unnecessary work at debuginfo=0; the std build uses the override so its MIR stays stable regardless of host debuginfo settings.",
    "testStrategy": "Use MIR-dump tests with two compilations of the same source differing only in debug info: (1) `-Zinline-mir -C debuginfo=0`: verify the inlined callee contributes no `debug <var> => <place>` entries in the caller's inlined scope while the CFG/statements are otherwise unchanged; (2) `-C debuginfo=full`: verify those callee `debug` entries do appear. Add a third run with `-Zinline-mir-preserve-debug -C debuginfo=0` and confirm the callee debug entries are preserved, mirroring std bootstrap behavior. Prefer existing `tests/mir-opt/inline` `EMIT_MIR` tests so one source differs only in flags; keep runtime/behavior checks separate because debug metadata is not semantically observable.",
